Kandor - patch 8: user-client selector redirects also for Navi (OCLP's old AMDRadeonX6000.kext on Tahoe)
Apply after patches 1-7. Author: ne1rom, with assistance from Claude (Anthropic)
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only

On Tahoe, OCLP's Navi userland calls AMDRadeonX6000_AMDAccelSharedUserClient with Tahoe's numbering, like the Vega
userland in patch 5: 0x102 with 1 scalar (getIOSurfaceInfo, old 0x103) and 0x105 with a 12-byte packet
(RsrcAndXorByteFlag, old 0x106). Measured on Tahoe 26.7.3 / OCLP 3.0.0-rc.5 with an RX 6900 XT: ~14000
"inputCount count mismatch 0x1 0x0" per 2 minutes and a solid-colour desktop without the redirect. Extends patch
5 to the X6000 class with the same detection (ForceLegacyMode symbol present = old kext); same -krynoredirect
switch. The same remap was validated earlier as ne1rom's egpudma plugin (258->259, 261->262).

